## Content vs. code

This license covers the **source code** of ElectrifyCost (Astro components,
TypeScript engine, CSV data structure, build scripts, configurations).

The **written content** (FAQ answers, guide prose, site copy on
electrifycost.com) is © 2026 Martin Lashgari and is NOT released under MIT.
Forking the codebase to build a similar calculator-first site for a different
niche is encouraged. Republishing the editorial content verbatim is not.

The **calculator output values** (cost ranges, rebate amounts, state energy
prices, climate data) are derived from public-domain primary sources (IRS,
DOE, EIA, BLS, NREL, NEEP, ENERGY STAR). Those source URLs are cited at
/sources/ and the underlying public-domain data is freely reusable.
